Subject: [PATCH] Show what the controller's buttons do, and raise scenery with
 it, on the PS5

The middle of the bottom toolbar, when it shows no news, lists what the buttons do right now:
PlayStation symbols and key caps with a word each, for the park, a window under the pointer
(with Tabs when it has them, Close when it can be closed), a dropdown, a radial menu, placing,
and building track or a bridge path. The title screen has them at the bottom.

While placing scenery that can be raised, up and down on the d-pad raise and lower it in height
steps (WindowSceneryRaise), as holding Shift and moving the mouse does, while the pointer keeps
moving it about. Triangle no longer opens the park windows while a tool is active, and Circle
closes an error message on the way rather than stopping at it.

The pointer follows the game's controller settings: the dead zone, and the sensitivity, which
scales its speed as it does scrolling.
